From: Aegir <aegir@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] raise the RISC-V qemu elfloader start address

The user image sits just above the kernel and grows up into the elfloader at
IMAGE_START_ADDR. The initrd's boot services have grown past 0x81000000, so
the elfloader is moved up (still below the DTB OpenSBI loads at 0x82200000).
---
 cmake-tool/helpers/application_settings.cmake | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/cmake-tool/helpers/application_settings.cmake
+++ b/cmake-tool/helpers/application_settings.cmake
@@ -60,7 +60,13 @@
     # But the RISC-V kernel is currently loaded to a different
     # address than what's modelled by the shoehorn.py tool.
     # So force the start address to one that works.
-    set(IMAGE_START_ADDR 0x81000000 CACHE INTERNAL "" FORCE)
+    #
+    # Aegir (third_party/patches/tools/seL4/0001): the user image is placed just
+    # above the kernel and grows up into the elfloader at this address. The
+    # initrd's boot services have grown past 0x81000000, so the elfloader is
+    # moved up -- still below the DTB OpenSBI loads at 0x82200000 -- to keep the
+    # image clear of it.
+    set(IMAGE_START_ADDR 0x81400000 CACHE INTERNAL "" FORCE)
   endif()
   if(KernelPlatformStar64)
     set(UseRiscVOpenSBI OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
